cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated manuscript and the archived software release."
title: "Home-care accessibility in Japan: open-source geospatial workflow"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fukuhara
    given-names: Satoshi
  - family-names: Ono
    given-names: Yohei
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-29
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Six-script R/OSRM workflow for nationwide potential spatial accessibility
  analyses comparing a 16-km criterion with road-network travel-time scenarios,
  including unique-centroid QC, population weighting, network-snapping
  sensitivity analyses, same-facility rerouting, and diagnostic CSIS
  address-matching quality-control summaries.
